  <layout>One page of text, with running head and page number at the top right, and catchword and signature at the foot. No marginal notes.</layout>
  <page_number>67</page_number>
  <running_head>an den Sünder,</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Zum</catchword>
    <signature>E ij</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Septem sunt, quæ frequenter præ oculis</l>
    <l n="2">ha-bere debemus.</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="3" para="true">Primum:</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">Peccatorum nostrorum, quæ fecimus,</l>
    <l n="5">mul-tiplicitas.</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="3" para="true">Secundum:</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Miserae nostrae vitæ brevitas.</l>
    <l n="8" type="heading" level="3" para="true">Tertium:</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Hominis mira instabilitas.</l>
    <l n="10" type="heading" level="3" para="true">Quartum:</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Horæ mortis nostræ incertitudo.</l>
    <l n="12" type="heading" level="3" para="true">Quintum:</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Altissimi Dei nostri judicatio.</l>
    <l n="14" type="heading" level="3" para="true">Sextum:</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">Tormentorum Inferni amaritudo.</l>
    <l n="16" type="heading" level="3" para="true">Septimum:</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Aeternæ gloriæ privatio.</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">
      <i>Hæc nota diligenter</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>&amp; minus peccabis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20" type="heading" level="2" para="true">
      <bl>Das ist zu Teutsch:</bl>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <bl>Es sind sieben dinge / die wir offt vor</bl>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <bl>augen haben sollen.</bl>
    </l>
    <l n="23" type="heading" level="3" para="true">
      <bl>Vors erst.</bl>
    </l>
    <l n="24" para="true">
      <bl>Die mannigfaltigkeit unser Sünden /</bl>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <bl>die wir</bl>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <bl>begangen haben.</bl>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Red ink underlining and strokes under several Latin lines (e.g. "vitæ brevitas", "nostræ incertitudo", "amaritudo", "privatio") and small pen marks are reader's markings, not print, and are omitted. The German text is set entirely in black letter; the Latin is roman with italics. The printed "vnser" is read as "unser" under the u/v rule. Labels such as "Primum:" are treated as level 3 headings because they are set apart, centred and italic.</notes>
</page>
